  "headline": "The corrected B outlet-pressure profile did not stop the same iteration-197 runaway. The D outlet-extension run stayed below the runaway screen through 3000 steady iterations and E through 9000, but neither met the configured SIMPLE convergence criteria. This is an unsettled, single-phase prescribed-flow diagnostic, not an accepted hydraulic reference, cavitation result, or full-tank discharge fix.",
  "scope_and_limits": [
    "Steady SIMPLE iteration labels are solver iteration counts, not physical seconds.",
    "Q=0.599812435 m3/s was derived from earlier CFD; it is not measured and is not an outlet-history boundary condition for the pressurized apparatus.",
    "D/E add a 0.30 m downstream numerical extension, 4608 cells and no-slip side-wall faces while moving the pressure boundary to a flat x=5.10 m plane. The result cannot isolate outlet distance alone as the cause.",
    "D and E end at iteration caps without a SIMPLE solution-converged message. Their native pAbs minima and required heads are unsettled diagnostics only.",
    "The branch reference is incompressible, single-phase water. Cavitation is not modeled; do not interpret its pressure minimum as a cavitation prediction.",
    "No tank headspace, valve transient, air-filled downstream line, or unsteady discharge is represented."
  ],
